WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.367
-This is Kenan Thompson
right here.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.367
That's who
we're hanging out with.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Kenan.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:06.467
-Me.
-That's you.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.767
Dude, you're crushing it.
Congrats on the show.

00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:10.734
-Thank you, man.
-Do your kids --

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.033
How old are your kids now?
7?

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.601
-They are 7 and 3,
my sweet little girls.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:17.467
Georgia and Gianna.
-And do they know your stuff?

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.834
Do they know "good burger?"
Do they do know "SNL"?

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:23.634
-They know "SNL."

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:24.901
They're not supposed
to be up that late.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:28.501
But they catch it the next day.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.701
-But I want them to find, like,
"Good Burger" and all that stuff

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:33.434
kind of organically.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.000
I want their friends in school
to be like,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.467
"Y'all haven't seen
'Good Burger'?"

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.334
and let them, like, kind of
discover how awesome daddy was.

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.133
[ Laughter ]
-Or is.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.100
I mean, dude, do they watch
"Kenan," and be like,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.634
"Wait.
Dad, that's not your family."

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.434
-Yeah,
they get a little confused.

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:50.000
They're like, "So, wait.
Are they us, or are we them?"

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.033
[ Laughter ]
-Who is what?

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:54.400
Who is who?
-Only because they haven't met

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.701
because we started shooting
in the middle of a pandemic.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:59.234
So, I mean, shout-out
to my cast and crew,

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.334
because we've been building
something pretty awesome

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.501
in some pretty dire situations.
You know?

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.200
-Yeah, thank you.
-I would send them

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.067
all the love in the world.
[ Applause ]

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.701
-I don't know
if I congratulated you

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.801
on getting nominated
for an Emmy for "Kenan."

00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:14.501
Congratulations.
-Thank you, man.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:15.901
Thank you, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.868
-Then got picked up, season two.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:20.701
-It's been an incredible
roller coaster of a time, man.

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.400
Like, you know,
got nominated for that,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.300
got nominated for "SNL,"
you know?

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.400
And it's just been
a very crazy time.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.067
Like, People's Choice
was like a four piece.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.734
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah. Four piece.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.934
-You know what I'm saying?
I'm nominated up.

00:01:31.934 --> 00:01:35.133
-How do you get time
to film the show and do "SNL"?

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:38.701
-It's all under NBC,
and Lorne makes it happen.

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:40.033
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.033
-He just controls it all.
-But, I mean,

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.767
do you know where you are
right now?

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:45.901
-This is -- Who are you?
You are James Fallon.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.467
-Yeah, James Fallon.
That's right.

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:50.834
I mean, we shoot, you know,
when "SNL" is off, kind of.

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:53.834
So we started in the summer,
and then "SNL" started,

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.734
so we took a break,
but then we only had, like,

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:57.667
a couple weeks to finish up,
so it overlapped a little bit.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.334
-Must be tough to do a sitcom.
-At the beginning,

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.133
it was like a five-piece
back and forth,

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:02.501
so that was too much.

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:04.634
And, yeah, it's a big switch.
You know what I mean?

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.000
Like, going from sketch
to sitcom,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.968
like going from thinking about
a million different ideas

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:10.467
to, like,
making a million different ideas

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:12.601
fit through one perspective.
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:15.000
-Yeah, and having a plot.
-I didn't mean to get

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.934
super deep about acting.
-No, you should.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:18.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.567
This is your Master Class
on acting.

00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.467
-Yeah, so, everybody buckle up.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.667
The key
to character development...

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.367
-No, no, no!
We don't have time.

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.801
-...when you're thinking about
backstories...

00:02:27.801 --> 00:02:31.067
-Season two, "Kenan,"
what do people have to know

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.434
if they hop into the show
Monday nights, on NBC?

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.767
-I think you need to know
that you can jump into the show

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:38.767
and have a laugh and not be lost
whenever you jump into it.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:40.133
It doesn't matter.
Like, that was one of

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.934
the biggest goals
is to, like, get to the funny.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:43.234
You know what I'm saying?
Like, we spent a lot of

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:44.767
the first season
explaining what it was,

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.033
and now we can
just explore these characters

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.200
and do whatever.
So whenever I, like,

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.968
watch a "Martin" marathon,
it doesn't matter, like,

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.100
what point of the episode
I catch it,

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.968
I just know, like,
for the rest of this time,

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.968
I'm gonna enjoy Martin Lawrence.
-There you go.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:03:01.033
So that's the way to -- good way
to plug Martin Lawrence.

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.934
-Thanks. I got to bring
Martin Lawrence up.

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.300
-We're going from "Martin"
to "Kenan."

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.400
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's Kenan Thompson

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.334
in the new season of "Kenan."
Take a look at this.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:10.667
-Kenan, Lawrence.
-Wow.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.767
I was thinking, like,
maybe I deserve a little fun.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:16.567
So I might be ready
to get on that app

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.567
and Impromptu Vous, too.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:21.834
-Ooh, well, well, well!
Welcome to the Booty Dome!

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.467
-Keep your voice down.
-Dating app?

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:25.834
Why would you want the profile
of somebody that tells you

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:27.968
everything about them before you
even go out with them?

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.300
-Uh, so you know
what you're getting into,

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.968
like a movie trailer.
-Where's the fun in that?

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:35.834
You know what I say?
Just enjoy the ride.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:40.100
-Sir, you -- you can't
just eat the produce.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:43.834
-Real life, 1; the ride, zero!

00:03:43.834 --> 00:03:46.133
-That's my man!
Kenan Thompson, everybody!

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:49.968
New episodes of "Kenan"
air Mondays at 8:00 p.m.

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:51.968
Every Monday
at 8:00 p.m. on NBC.

